     "text": "{\"cost\": 8, \"rationale\": \"The shortest path uses 8 techniques: (1) phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user; (2) pivot_internal gives reach_internal, since segmented is false; (3) auth_ciserver gives foothold_ciserver, since mfa_user is false; (4) escalate_ciserver gives admin_ciserver, since patched_ciserver is false; (5) leak_secrets_ciserver gives stolen_dbadmin; (6) auth_db gives foothold_db, since mfa_dbadmin is false; (7) escalate_db gives admin_db using stolen_dbadmin; (8) exfiltrate_db gives exfiltrated. No step can be dropped. Exfiltration needs admin on db, fileserver or backup. That requires a foothold there plus stolen_dbadmin, each taking one step. stolen_dbadmin needs admin_ciserver, admin_dc or admin_adfs. The ciserver route needs auth, escalate and leak, which is 3 steps. The dc and adfs routes are longer because they first need stolen_admin through kerberoasting from an internal server foothold. Reaching internal needs a foothold plus a pivot, and phishing supplies both the foothold and stolen_user in one step.\"}"
